// sin with a period of 2 (sin(pi * v)) and its output normalised to 0...1.
// Sims (1991, section 4.1) mentions versions of sin and cos that normalise
// their results to 0...1. Figure 13 is the only bundled figure that calls
// sin. Plain sin(v) there gave a left-to-right ramp, from the "+ x" term,
// clipped to black on the left. A sweep of periods 1, 2, 3, 4 and 2*pi
// found 2 the only one without the ramp that still gave Karl's brown and
// blue palette and local darks (1 over-saturates, 4 and up bring back the
// ramp). cos is unchanged: Figures 6 and 12 use it and were not re-checked.
// See Documentation/Figure13.md.
node "sin"(v0) {
	return (sin(v0 * 3.14159265) + float3(1.0)) * 0.5
}
